      "id": "2b",
      "title": "The same set, after fixes by class",
      "status": "done",
      "date": "2026-11-07",
      "kind": "eval",
      "test_set": "Round 2's devices, faults and seeds, with three fixes made by class and the same prompts for every model: a check against a value needs a quoted manual line or a named spec, or the plan is refused before anything moves; a part that doesn't move at its normal force limit is the finding, so a retest keeps the same limit; and a skill called as a tool is pointed at plans. Errors are now drawn from the seed and what each action is (an explore stage, or a skill on a target, and which time it has run), so two models that run the same step meet the same error. This round ran from a frozen copy of the repo made at 2026-11-07 17:13:01 EST, because other work was changing System 1 at the time. With the new draw, 5% per action gave one error in eight model runs (a slow arm on a retest), so this round says little about recovery.",
      "spend": "436,287 tokens across the four models, plus 61,000 for one confirming run after a fourth fix.",
      "takeaway": "No false findings from any model, and every model found both faults. Each model had one plan turned down for a made-up limit, and fixed it before anything moved. One new class showed up in all four: calling finish_run while the routine still held at its last failed step. Now finish_run closes it when nothing is left to run, confirmed on a rerun with no refused call. One noise flag remains: Grok's dial missed once (stopped on travel at 2.9 N), then passed, so it settled as intermittent. Grok read it as a miss, but System 1's rule calls that miss failed, not inconclusive, so it's for System 1's rules rather than the harness.",
